&Q000498 = An adab to Enlil for Būr-Suen (Būr-Suen B)
@composite
#project: ucsl/etcsl
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.5.7.2
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.5.7.2&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div segment A

@div unknown A

A.A.1. [...] X an ki-še₃ dili-ni dib
#lem: X; X; an[sky]; ki[place]; dili[single]; dib[pass]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.1

A.A.2. saŋ# il₂! palil {d}a-nun-na-ke₄-ne
#lem: saŋ[head]; il[raise]; palil[first and foremost]; Anunak[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.2

A.A.3. ka-ta e₃-a-ni sag₂ nu-di#
#lem: kag[mouth]; e[leave]; sag[scatter]; di[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.3

A.A.4. {d}nu-nam-nir eš-bar dug₄-ga nu-kur₂-ru
#lem: Nunamnir[1]DN; ešbar[decision]; dug[speak]; kur[different]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.4

A.A.5. saŋ-kug-ŋal₂ ni₂ su zig₃ ri-a
#lem: saŋguŋal[proud]; ni[fear]; su[flesh]; zig[rise]; ri[impose]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.5

A.A.6. (1:dili-a-ni-še₃ saŋ il₂:1) nun-gal-e-ne
#lem: dili[single]; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; Nungal[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.6

:6v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) [dili-a]-ni il₂ saŋ-kal
#lem: dili[single]; il[raise]; saŋkal[foremost]

A.A.7. eš₃ nibru{ki} dur-an-ki-a-ka
#lem: eš[shrine]; Nibru[1]SN; Durankik[1]TN
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.7

A.A.8. e₂-kur e₂ nam tar-tar-re-da
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; e[house]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.8

A.A.9. [e₂] kug za-gin₃-na dur₂ bi₂-in-ŋar#
#lem: e[house]; kug[metal]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; dur[buttocks]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.9

A.A.10. [ama] {d}nin-lil₂ kur gal-da zag ša₄
#lem: ama[mother]; Ninlil[1]DN; kur[mountain(s)]; gal[big]; zag[side]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.10

A.A.11. [X X] X-a-ni gu₂-da u₃-mu-ni-in-la₂
#lem: X; X; X; gu[neck]; la[hang]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.11

A.A.12. [...] X inim mu-na-ab-dug₄-ge
#lem: X; X; inim[word]; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.12

A.A.13. [...] šag₄#-ge pad₃-da# [...]
#lem: X; šag[heart]; pad[find]; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.A.13

$ (unknown no. of lines missing)
@end unknown

@end segment

@div segment B

@div sa-ŋara B

B.B.1. iri a₂ aŋ₂ [...]
#lem: iri[city]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]; X
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.1

B.B.2. zu₂ keše₂-bi [...]
#lem: zu[tooth]; kešed[bind]; X
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.2

B.B.3. {d}en-lil₂-me-en dug₄-ga-[zu] mah#-am₃
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; dug[speak]; mah[great]
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.3

B.B.4. diŋir na-me nu-mu-e-da-bur₂#-re
#lem: diŋir[deity]; name[any]; bur[spread out]
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.4

B.B.5. nam# i-ri-tar pa e₃ ga-mu-ra-ab-dirig
#lem: nam[fate]; tar[cut]; pa[branch]; e[leave]; dirig[make more than]
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.5

B.B.6. nam-til₃-zu nam-til₃ ga-mu-ra-ab-tah
#lem: namtil[life]; namtil[life]; tah[add]
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.6

B.B.7. {d}utu-gin₇ ud-zu ga-ra-ab-sud-su₃-ud
#lem: Utu[1]DN; ud[sun]; sud[distant]
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.7

B.B.8. kur-kur-ra diŋir-bi za-e-me-en
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; diŋir[deity]; zaʾe[you]
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.8

@div trailer 

B.B.9. sa-ŋar-ra-am₃
#lem: saŋara[musical notation]
#etcsl: line-id=B.B.9

@end trailer

@end sa-jara

@div ŋišgiŋal C

B.C.10. en nam tar-re-me-en {d}bur-{d}suen ŋiškim lugal mu-e-til₃-le-en
#lem: en[lord]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; Bursuenak[1]RN; ŋeškim[sign]; lugal[king]; til[live (of a single person)]
#etcsl: line-id=B.C.10

@div trailer 

B.C.11. ŋiš-gi₄-ŋal₂-bi-im
#lem: ŋešgiŋal[musical refrain]
#etcsl: line-id=B.C.11

@end trailer

@end jicgijal

@div uru D

B.D.12. niŋ₂-zid niŋ₂-gen₆-na pa bi₂-a-e₃ su kalam-ma mu-[dug₃]
#lem: niŋzid[righteousness]; niŋgina[truth]; pa[branch]; e[leave]; su[flesh]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; dug[good]
#etcsl: line-id=B.D.12

B.D.13. {d}bur-{d}suen X AB ud šu₂-uš mu-zu he₂-em-hul₂#
#lem: Bursuenak[1]RN; X; X; ud[sun]; šuš[cover]; mu[name]; hul[rejoice]
#etcsl: line-id=B.D.13

B.D.14. [X X] E NE saŋ-zu he₂-ni-in-il₂ en saŋ-bi-še₃ he₂-pad₃
#lem: X; X; X; X; saŋ[head]; il[raise]; en[lord]; saŋ[head]; pad[find]
#etcsl: line-id=B.D.14

@div trailer 

B.D.15. [u₁₈-ru₁₂-bi-im]
#lem: uru[literary subscript]
#etcsl: line-id=B.D.15

@end trailer

@end uru

@div trailer 

B.D.16. [a]-da#-ab {d}en-lil₂-la₂-kam#
#lem: adab[drum]; Enlil[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=B.D.16

#etcsl#doc lines 15 and 16 are written as one line in source

@end trailer

@end segment








@translation labeled en project









#lg A	unknown


@(A.A.1 = 1-13) …… who alone surpasses heaven and earth, the exalted one, prominent among the @wDN{Anuna} gods, whose utterances cannot be overturned! @wDN{Nunamnir}, whose decisions cannot be altered, proud one imbued with terrifying awesomeness,  @varh[t2572.v1]{who alone is exalted } @vart[t2572.v2,t2572.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} who alone is eminent, the foremost one } among the Great Princes, has taken his seat in the shrine of @wSN{Nibru}, in @wTN{Dur-an-ki}, in @wTN{E-kur}, the temple where the fates are determined, in the holy shining temple. When Mother @wDN{Ninlil}, who is equal in rank with the Great Mountain, embraces him ……, …… says to ……: @q[Ninlil,]{“…… chosen in the heart by …….”}  @gap{unknown no. of lines missing} 

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t2572.v1 t2572.v2
#etcsl#altGrpc

#lg B	sa-jara


@(B.B.1 = 1-8) The city, where …… orders …….  @gap{1 line fragmentary}  @wDN{Enlil}, what you say is exalted, and there is no god who can interpret it. @q[Enlil,]{“I will make the fate I have determined for you even more glorious. I will make your life long-lasting. I will make your days as numerous as those of @wDN{Utu}.”} You are the god of all the foreign lands!

#trailer rubric	sa-jara


@(B.B.9 = 9) @fsux{Sa-ŋara}.

#lg C	jicgijal


@(B.C.10 = 10) You are the lord who determines the fates! @wRN{Būr-@wDN{Suen's}} royal trust is in you!

#trailer rubric	jicgijal


@(B.C.11 = 11) Its @fsux{ŋišgiŋal}.

#lg D	uru


@(B.D.12 = 12-14) You have made justice and righteousness conspicuous, and you have made the Land feel content. @wRN{Būr-@wDN{Suen}}, may your name be a cause for rejoicing …… daily. May you be exalted among ……; let them call you the pre-eminent lord!

#trailer rubric	uru


@(B.D.15 = 15) Its @fsux{uru}.

#trailer subscript	adab


@(B.D.16 = 16) An @fsux{adab} of @wDN{Enlil}. @notep{lines 15 and 16 are written as one line in source}



